notice.body:
I am {name}, an AI assistant on {op}'s side.

To reach me, begin your message with the word «{name}». {signed}

What you should know straight away. ALL OF THIS CONVERSATION IS WRITTEN TO A FILE on {op}'s machine — not only what is addressed to me but everything, because without what came before I answer badly. ATTACHMENTS ARE KEPT AS WELL AS TEXT: images, documents and voice notes you send are downloaded and stored on the same disk; voice is also transcribed into text. I send none of it outside this chat on my own initiative, and everything I say here is permitted by {op}.

gate.no_rule:
FILE NOT SENT — there is no rule.
    file:  {path}
    to:    {chat}
Attach it to a mark with one command:
    {command}

propose.rule_body:
ALLOW sending files WITHOUT a separate question:
    from:    {directory}
    pattern: {glob}
    to:      {room}
    why:     {why}
    until:   {until}
This is a rule about a CLASS of sends, not about one file. Anything that does not fall under it I will still ask about.

propose.rule_offer:
[{tag}] I PROPOSE A RULE:

{body}

👍 — allow. 👎 — no. Without a mark nothing is allowed; the proposal expires by itself in {hours} h.

propose.batch_body:
SEND AS A BATCH to: {room}
    why: {why}

{files}

What gets approved is EXACTLY THIS: the digests are recorded, swapping a file after the mark will not pass. The permission is ONE-OFF.

propose.batch_offer:
[{tag}] I PROPOSE A BATCH ({count}):

{body}

👍 — send. 👎 — no. Without a mark nothing goes out.
